    "Speaker / Participant / Moderator": "Mr. Akshay Surve (Speaker)",
    "Company Name": "Anthropic",
    "Location / Room": "Cube",
    "Tracks": "",
    "Description": "Most AI pilots don't fail because the model is weak; they fail because nobody defined what \"good\" looks like before shipping. Evaluations, or evals, turn fuzzy goals like \"accurate\", \"compliant\" or \"safe\" into measurable tests that tell you whether an AI system is ready for production and whether it stays that way. This masterclass covers how to build evals first: writing the eval as the spec before the agent, turning real failures into a small golden set, layering code checks, LLM judges and human review, and grading agents on outcome while tracking the path they took\n\nApplicable to anyone building with LLMs and agents. An ideal kickstart; no prior evals experience needed",
